course: dictionary
lesson: 2543
title: Defer: putting things off
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Defer» is a formal word, the kind you find in letters, school notices and exams. It means to put something off until later, so it does not happen now. «The meeting was deferred until next week.» The meeting did not happen today. It was moved to a later time.
explain: The words around it give you clues. «Until next week» tells you the meeting moved to later. Check by swapping in an everyday word: put off or postpone. If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: The second meaning is «defer to». «I defer to your experience» means I accept your opinion because you know more than I do. Nothing is being put off here. You are showing respect. Context tells you which meaning is which.
fact: Defer means to put something off until later.
fact: Defer to means to accept someone else's opinion or decision because you respect them.
fact: «Deferred» is the past tense of defer: «The trip was deferred.»
fact: Put off and postpone are everyday words that mean nearly the same as defer's first meaning.
fact: «Deferred success» is a joking UK phrase for failure; it is a joke, not the real meaning of defer.
exercise: «The school deferred the trip until the weather improved.» What does deferred mean here? | Moved to a different country | *Put off until later | Hurried forward to today | Cancelled for ever and never talked about
exercise: Ella says, «I defer to Dad, he knows more about cars.» What does defer to mean? | Argue with Dad until he gives up | *Accept Dad's opinion because he knows more | Tell Dad to sell the car | Ignore Dad and drive off
exercise: Which word is closest in meaning to defer? | Remember | *Postpone | Hurry | Shout
test: «The teacher deferred the test because it was raining hard.» Deferred is closest to which word? | Finished | Shouted | *Postponed | Forgotten
test: «She defers to the captain when the team has to choose.» What does defers to mean? | *Respects his decision and accepts it | Takes over the team herself | Forgets the captain exists | Argues with the captain loudly
exam: Which sentence uses defer to mean put off until later? | «Dad deferred to my choice of pizza.» | *«We deferred the sports day until the field was dry.» | «The children deferred their ideas to the teacher.» | «I defer to your experience.»
